select 've-pricing-points-passport', 'vegans-explore', 'Logan', $pb$BUILD RECORD, 2026-11-01 (Logan). Earn your Passport, part 5 built and live, both switches OFF until Sean turns them on (Sean: "Approved, go with your defaults and build it").
5a. THE BUSINESS OFFER. Depot > Passport Challenge stops > Offers we send: New offer makes the offer and its own tracked link; Send it sends the offer email by hand, always. With the follow-up switch on, two days later on a weekday from 10 AM Eastern: "Your spot is still open" if the link was never clicked, "What a stop really costs" if it was. Applying marks it Applied; no answer two days after the follow-up puts it in the Inbox for the chapter's Community Manager. Stop these emails adds a suppression. The apply confirmation is the new "You applied" email (ve-vault).
5b. NOT-READY-YET EMAILS. Depot > Challenges > Taster emails: with the switch on, Day 3 this week in their city, Day 7 an episode for why they came, Day 14 their suggested Guide, then the Daily Pulse every Thursday, and December 1, 18 and 30 the Founding deadline notes; never two within six days; paying, earning a membership or unsubscribing ends it.
From VEGANS EXPLORE <hello@vegansexplore.com>, signed Vegans Explore team, replies to contact@lesaruss.com. Migration 20261101_earn_your_passport_emails.sql (through ve-once-challenges, now the 410 stub); ve-nurture from commit 6cff6e0 and ve-vault from 91c8c26 (sha256 matched). Proven live with [TEST] offers outside sending hours (previews, guards, Applied, the Inbox, the stop link), both Depot views on desktop and phone; every test row removed. Not yet proven: a real follow-up and Taster email going out.
LOGAN'S DEFAULTS, SEAN'S TO CHANGE: the sender and signature, 10 AM Eastern, weekdays for businesses, Thursdays for the Pulse, the December dates.
NEXT: 6. the content gig, 7. the business points rule.$pb$, 'text', 'decision'
